        "A negative answer to Nevo's homology-sphere decomposition question \u2014 Alec Kriebel, v1.0.0 (2026-10-17). Problem30000214, Nevo OWR17/2005 Problem8 printed961; DCG39(2008) Problem3.7 printed417. Full negative answer: finite pure2D abstract K is doubly Cohen-Macaulay over every characteristic-zero field but contains no2D homology-sphere subcomplex over any field, including all face links. No subdivision or enlargement. Explicit affine-building congruence quotient modulo t^9; unchanged PG(2,11) links; all vertex deletions via weighted spectral argument; Euler obstruction excludes spheres. LSV construction, Lubotzky-Meshulam degree/congruence method, Ballmann-Swiatkowski vanishing and Januszkiewicz-Swiatkowski curvature credited. Bounded176queryinputs/167exactstrings found no verified earlier recorded full target; unread Chari1997/Baclawski1982 and other source/corpus gaps disclosed, no firstness/current-global-openness certificate. Extensive AI assistance; unrefereed, no external human peer review or formal certification. Two successive fresh no-history complete-package reviews passed identical release. Complete finite positives normal/optimized,6actual mathematical failures; optional normal-only NumPy diagnostic, no full quotient enumeration. https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1155 Published record: https://zenodo.org/records/23444839"
